q 1 0 0 1 48 509.8898 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 18 TL/F2 14 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 4 Tm (7. Biopsy coverage and exported metadata)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 48 453.8898 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 12 TL/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 26 Tm (Executed SQL results show 458 records marked biopsied \(42.1%\): 273 BCC, 56 SCC, 17 MEL, 95 ACK, 12 NEV)Tj T* (and 5 SEK. All 346 BCC/SCC/MEL records are marked biopsied. Biopsy status is metadata; the underlying)Tj T* (pathology reports and label provenance were not reviewed.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 48 379.8898 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 12 TL/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 50 Tm (The exported CSV contains 1,088 rows and 21 columns. It retains patient and lesion IDs for audit and)Tj T* (traceability, excludes biopsy status and image filenames, and converts zero-coded measurements to nulls. The)Tj T* (script comment claiming identifiers are excluded is inconsistent with its SELECT statement: IDs are retained in)Tj T* (the export and must be excluded from model predictors. diagnostic and malignant_proxy are alternative target)Tj T* (labels; neither should predict the other. The export is prepared metadata, not a trained or validated model.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 48 341.8898 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 18 TL/F2 14 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 4 Tm (8. Recommendations)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 48 213.8898 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 12 TL/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 98 Tm (1. Confirm the record-count discrepancy and lesion ID convention with the data provider; retain original records)Tj T* (and use the unique patient/lesion pair for traceability.)Tj T* (2. Improve recording of skin type and both diameters, and investigate why measurement completeness varies by)Tj T* (diagnosis.)Tj T* (3. Investigate the observed age, symptom and exposure associations with adjusted analysis and suitable)Tj T* (independent data before drawing clinical or causal conclusions.)Tj T* (4. For future modelling, verify labels, address missing values within training folds, encode categorical variables,)Tj T* (exclude IDs and biopsy status from predictors, and assess class imbalance. No model training is required by the)Tj T* (explicit SQL workflow.)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 48 175.8898 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 18 TL/F2 14 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 4 Tm (9. Limitations and conclusion)Tj T* ET Q q 1 0 0 1 48 83.88976 cm 0 0 0 rg BT 12 TL/F1 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 0 62 Tm (The analysis is descriptive and unadjusted. Sampling, recruitment and label provenance are not established;)Tj T* (findings cannot be generalised to the population or interpreted causally. Repeated lesion IDs and substantial,)Tj T* (diagnosis-dependent missingness limit interpretation. Some small groups contain few observations. SQL joins,)Tj T* (summaries and quality checks address the brief, and the export supports further preparation. The most frequent)Tj T* (label is ACK; BCC/SCC/MEL proportions vary by age, exposure and lesion features. Reliable further research)Tj T* (depends on clarifying identifiers and improving measurement completeness.)Tj T* ET Q Q
